---
/**
 * Security awareness — `/services/security-awareness/`. The wedge page, per
 * docs/copy/security-awareness.md. Highest-priority page from the SEO audit —
 * title/description target the compliance keyword cluster directly.
 */
import '../../styles/global.css';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Reveal from '../../components/Reveal.astro';

const included = [
  {
    title: 'Monthly phishing simulation',
    body: 'Campaigns run against your own staff, with results formatted for the report your regulator actually asks for.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Remedial training',
    body: 'Anyone who fails a simulation is enrolled automatically. Completion is tracked and evidenced.',
  },
  {
    title: 'New-joiner onboarding',
    body: 'Security induction from day one, so the evidence trail starts when the person does.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Quarterly content refresh',
    body: 'Awareness material updated against a plan built for your institution, not a generic library.',
  },
];
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Close the staff-security-awareness audit finding without a per-seat US-dollar licence. Monthly phishing simulation, automatic remedial training, and reporting built for the Bank of Zambia's Cyber and Information Risk Management Guidelines."
    />
    <title>Security Awareness & Phishing Simulation for Zambian Lenders | Nexus Consulting</title>
  </head>
  <body class="bg-paper text-ink">
    <Nav />

    <main>
      <Section ground="dark" id="wedge-header">
        <Reveal as="div">
          <p class="chip">Security & compliance</p>
          <h1 class="mt-4 font-display font-bold text-balance" style="font-size: var(--text-5); max-width: 22ch">
            Closing the audit finding without a per-seat licence
          </h1>

          <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2" style="max-width: var(--content-max)">
            <p style="color: var(--steel)">
              Every regulated lender in Zambia carries some version of the same finding:
              staff security awareness is not being measured, and there is nothing on file
              to prove otherwise. It is one of the areas the Bank of Zambia's Cyber and
              Information Risk Management Guidelines (gazetted 31 May 2023) expect a
              supervised institution to show evidence for.
            </p>
            <p style="color: var(--steel)">
              The platforms built to close it are priced per seat in US dollars. For a
              sixty-person microfinance institution that is not a budget line, so the
              finding rolls forward to the next examination, and the one after that.
            </p>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-6 max-w-[65ch]" style="color: var(--steel)">
            The affordable version already exists. Our managing consultant built it on
            open-source foundations and ran it inside a Bank of Zambia-supervised
            institution, where it closed the finding it was commissioned to close. That
            programme is what Nexus now deploys and operates for clients. There is no
            per-seat fee, so the cost does not climb with headcount and carries no forex
            exposure.
          </p>
        </Reveal>
      </Section>

      <Section ground="light" id="included">
        <Reveal as="div">
          <p class="chip">What's included</p>
          <h2 class="mt-4 font-display font-bold text-balance" style="font-size: var(--text-4)">
            Four things, running every month
          </h2>
        </Reveal>

        <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
          {included.map((item) => (
            <Reveal as="div" class="included-card">
              <h3 class="font-display font-semibold" style="font-size: var(--text-1)">{item.title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2" style="color: var(--slate)">{item.body}</p>
            </Reveal>
          ))}
        </div>

        <blockquote class="callout mt-10">
          <p style="font-weight: 600">Where the fee actually goes.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            The platform being open source is what removes the licence. It does not remove
            the work. Running the campaigns each month, producing the regulator-facing
            report and refreshing the content each quarter is the retainer — and it is
            precisely the part an institution without a dedicated security function cannot
            do for itself.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
      </Section>

      <Section ground="dark" id="adjacent">
        <Reveal as="div">
          <p class="max-w-[65ch]" style="color: var(--steel)">
            Two engagements follow from the same conversation and are often bought
            together. <strong style="color: var(--paper)">Microsoft 365 tenant hardening</strong>
            enforces MFA, configures Defender, and sets the Exchange and Conditional Access
            policy that stops the phishing which gets through despite training.
            <strong style="color: var(--paper)">Firewall hardening with site-to-site VPN</strong>
            reviews and tightens a FortiGate or Sophos estate, and links branches securely
            to head office.
          </p>
          <a href="/services/" class="btn btn-ghost mt-8">See all services</a>
        </Reveal>
      </Section>

      <Section ground="light" id="proof">
        <Reveal as="div">
          <p class="chip">Proof</p>
          <p class="mt-6 max-w-[65ch]" style="color: var(--slate)">
            Our managing consultant designed, deployed and ran a phishing-simulation and
            awareness programme on open-source foundations, integrated with the
            institution's directory and mail platform. It closed the regulatory finding it
            was commissioned for. This is the programme Nexus now deploys for clients.
          </p>
          <div class="callout callout-light mt-6">
            <p style="font-weight: 600">Why this is unnamed.</p>
            <p class="mt-2">
              The institution is identifiable to anyone in the sector and the work touched
              their control environment. We do not publish that without written consent. If
              you are seriously evaluating the programme we will arrange the conversation
              directly.
            </p>
          </div>
        </Reveal>
      </Section>

      <Section ground="dark" id="close">
        <Reveal as="div">
          <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-balance" style="font-size: var(--text-4); max-width: 20ch">
            Start with the scoping call.
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-[55ch]" style="color: var(--steel)">
            Thirty minutes, no charge, no obligation. We'll tell you plainly whether this
            closes your finding.
          </p>
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary mt-8">Book a scoping call</a>
        </Reveal>
      </Section>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .included-card {
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    background: var(--mist);
  }

  .callout {
    max-width: 60ch;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--paper) 8%, transparent);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--paper) 18%, transparent);
  }

  .callout-light {
    background: var(--mist);
    border: 1px solid var(--mist);
    color: var(--slate);
  }
</style>
